"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395299-who-do-you-think-mithras\u2019s-true-love-is#post1395299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A. Roger de Camden (they\u2019ve been together a while)<br /> <br /> B. Kemintiri (she did give him that ring)<br /> <br /> C. The Toreador Melusine (opposites attract...)<br /> <br /> D. No one (he\u2019s mostly just out for himself)<br /> <br /> He\u2019s one of my favorite characters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> D, Mithras is an old selfish megalomaniac who hijacked a religion in order to make himself a god and became convinced he actually was...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T05:24:18-07:00","id":1395314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395299-who-do-you-think-mithras\u2019s-true-love-is?p=1395302#post1395302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> Both very good points. Thanks.<br /> <br /> Mithras was Embraced by Veddartha/Ventrue around 1200 BCE, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The date of his embrace is listed as 1258 BCE. Note that there's a fair share of controversy about who his sire was/is. Veddartha is a 4th generation vampire and it's been speculated Mithras was embraced as a 5th generation vampire before he lowered his generation through diablerie.<br /> <br /> The fact he met with Haqim in 121 CE in the Antediluvian's last recorded appearance gives some credit to the notion he was a diablerist, possibly committing the deed by following the tenets of the Road of Blood.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T05:37:09-07:00","id":1395319,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24992\" data-vbnamecard=\"24992\">Haquim</a> fascinating! Thank you. And thanks for answering. I do think Roger and Kemintiri loved him though, even if he doesn\u2019t love them back. (Not sure about Melusine, I think that might\u2019ve just been a mutual fling.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T06:02:05-07:00","id":1395323,"title":"","content":"He also was lovers with Queen Anne Bowesley.<br /> <br /> So much for vampires not having sex.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yes, I think vampires are very good for centuries-long polygamy.<br /> <br /> Lucita was deeply intimate lovers with Fatima and Anatole both after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T07:19:20-07:00","id":1395341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395299-who-do-you-think-mithras\u2019s-true-love-is?p=1395319#post1395319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24992\" data-vbnamecard=\"24992\">Haquim</a> fascinating! Thank you. And thanks for answering. I do think Roger and Kemintiri loved him though, even if he doesn\u2019t love them back. (Not sure about Melusine, I think that might\u2019ve just been a mutual fling.)</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Fall of London Lord Cadmen surely does. Kemintiri is Mithras' equal though... she may love him in her own way, but we are talking about a 3.300 years old 4th generation Vampire whose ultimate goal is to kill her own sire, the antediluvian Set, who once caused Mithras himself to go mad. Also bear in mind that Mithras is a master of dominate and presence, which make him able to make others feel like they are deeply in love with him (or adoration of him).<br /> <br /> More importantly your post raises an interesting question: what is &quot;love&quot; for beings who have existed for thousands of years and think of themselves as gods? The answer is very significant for the autcome of the topic at hand here, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T09:13:48-07:00","id":1395361,"title":"","content":"You both raise some really good points. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T10:08:03-07:00","id":1395386,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't think that vampires that old are capable of love<br /> The blood of Caine is really not conducive to true love when every emotion can be manufactured through Dominate, Presence or the Blood Bond.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395299-who-do-you-think-mithras\u2019s-true-love-is?p=1395323#post1395323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He also was lovers with Queen Anne Bowesley.<br /> <br /> So much for vampires not having sex.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yes, I think vampires are very good for centuries-long polygamy.<br /> <br /> Lucita was deeply intimate lovers with Fatima and Anatole both after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't Bowesley was his love so much as he was grooming her for it.<br /> <br /> Also, was Anatole Lucita's lover or just her mentor? And didn't she have a thing with Jan Pieterzoon?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T10:36:47-07:00","id":1395393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395299-who-do-you-think-mithras\u2019s-true-love-is?p=1395386#post1395386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I don't think that vampires that old are capable of love<br /> The blood of Caine is really not conducive to true love when every emotion can be manufactured through Dominate, Presence or the Blood Bond.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't Bowesley was his love so much as he was grooming her for it.<br /> <br /> Also, was Anatole Lucita's lover or just her mentor? And didn't she have a thing with Jan Pieterzoon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anatole was something quite different than a lover for Lucita. He was her morality anchor. Anatole was a self styled &quot;country priest&quot; with real faith (he had True Faith 1... I loathe vampires with TF but he had it) while her own sire was a prince of the church whose faith was shallow and tyrannical, besides him wanting to control Lucita in all things out of perverse &quot;love&quot; for her. That's why when Anatole died Lucita's humanity started slipping and she had to resort to paths.<br /> <br /> That said I don't recall reading anywhere Lucita and Anatole were lovers. She and Fatima for sure but Anatole was something quite different and possibly &quot;higher&quot; than a lover.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T10:42:42-07:00","id":1395394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395299-who-do-you-think-mithras\u2019s-true-love-is?p=1395386#post1395386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, was Anatole Lucita's lover or just her mentor? And didn't she have a thing with Jan Pieterzoon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I took their relationship as lovers from Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> Jan Pietszoon had a raging lust for her but it's never said if she reciprocated or even knew. I doubt it was uncommon for Elders and Neonates to have a thing for her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T11:28:07-07:00","id":1395403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395299-who-do-you-think-mithras\u2019s-true-love-is?p=1395314#post1395314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The date of his embrace is listed as 1258 BCE. Note that there's a fair share of controversy about who his sire was/is. Veddartha is a 4th generation vampire and it's been speculated Mithras was embraced as a 5th generation vampire before he lowered his generation through diablerie.<br /> <br /> The fact he met with Haqim in 121 CE in the Antediluvian's last recorded appearance gives some credit to the notion he was a diablerist, possibly committing the deed by following the tenets of the Road of Blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's based on the fact that the write-up or a fifth-generation vampire named Maltheas gave his sire as Veddartha. But we don't know for certain that they're the same Veddartha. (*cough* Hardestadt *cough*). The Wiki says it's Sanskrit for &quot;wise and prosperous one&quot;, so it's not a stretch to think that one of the Antediluvian's childer might have adopted the name from him. The Ventrue Antediluvian was rumored to have met Final Death before Mithras' Embrace, true, but the Tzimisce Antediluvian was <i>rumored </i>to have died during the Anarch revolt. <br /> <br /> The diablerist theory is plausible, but unproven for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T11:43:55-07:00","id":1395406,"title":"","content":"1: A lengthly succession of mortals<br /> 2: his sire. Like, how can anyone compete for affection with the OG ventrue? The guy doesn't have a single digit stat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T11:57:53-07:00","id":1395410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395299-who-do-you-think-mithras\u2019s-true-love-is?p=1395403#post1395403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's based on the fact that the write-up or a fifth-generation vampire named Maltheas gave his sire as Veddartha. But we don't know for certain that they're the same Veddartha. (*cough* Hardestadt *cough*). The Wiki says it's Sanskrit for &quot;wise and prosperous one&quot;, so it's not a stretch to think that one of the Antediluvian's childer might have adopted the name from him. The Ventrue Antediluvian was rumored to have met Final Death before Mithras' Embrace, true, but the Tzimisce Antediluvian was <i>rumored </i>to have died during the Anarch revolt.<br /> <br /> The diablerist theory is plausible, but unproven for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said there's controversy about Mithras original generation. And it's old. I can remember discussing this very same topic in 1998 on the Ex Libris Nocturnis Forums. All things considered there's no &quot;canon&quot; answer to Mithras original generation because the question was left unanswered on purpose. Personally I favor the idea he was 5th gen and then diablerized his way to 4th gen but I know that's not necessarily the &quot;truth&quot; about Mithras.<br /> <br /> As for the Ventrue antediluvian i think the only antediluvians who are dead and gone are Ravnos and possibly Cappadocius (if his spectre was put to rest, that is), the others all persist in some form, Ventrue included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 06-09-2020, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T11:58:48-07:00","id":1395411,"title":"","content":"There need be no contradiction in the generations of Mithras and Maltheas.<br /> <br /> In Beckett's Jyhad Diary, the Laibon talk about a process by which vampires with powerful blood can intentionally weaken their blood. As BJD was a fluff narrative and not crunchy mechanics, it's not clear whether this means generation or blood potency. Given blood potency, as a concept, hadn't been published in VtM at the time BJD was published, I'd guess it is the weakening of generation. Thus, a ninth generation vampire could somehow become a tenth generation vampire.<br /> <br /> So, it is possible that Veddhartha (childe of Ynosh, childe of Caine), known as the progenitor of the whole of Clan Ventrue and first of his generation, sired Mithras. Then, after siring him, Veddhartha weakened his own generation to fourth, because... reasons.<br /> <br /> So, Mithras was sired when Veddhartha was 3rd gen, and Maltheas was sired when Veddhartha was 4th gen.<br /> <br /> At least that's one possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T12:08:37-07:00","id":1395416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395299-who-do-you-think-mithras\u2019s-true-love-is?p=1395411#post1395411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There need be no contradiction in the generations of Mithras and Maltheas.<br /> <br /> In Beckett's Jyhad Diary, the Laibon talk about a process by which vampires with powerful blood can intentionally weaken their blood. As BJD was a fluff narrative and not crunchy mechanics, it's not clear whether this means generation or blood potency. Given blood potency, as a concept, hadn't been published in VtM at the time BJD was published, I'd guess it is the weakening of generation. Thus, a ninth generation vampire could somehow become a tenth generation vampire.<br /> <br /> So, it is possible that Veddhartha (childe of Ynosh, childe of Caine), known as the progenitor of the whole of Clan Ventrue and first of his generation, sired Mithras. Then, after siring him, Veddhartha weakened his own generation to fourth, because... reasons.<br /> <br /> So, Mithras was sired when Veddhartha was 3rd gen, and Maltheas was sired when Veddhartha was 4th gen.<br /> <br /> At least that's one possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>He would have had to strengthen his blood again before siring Alexander and Antonius, however.<br /> <br /> Also, regarding the sire of the Ventrue Antediluvian, Alexander names Enoch however, it's worth pointing out that in DA V20, some vampires got their hands on what was likely Irad's vitae and it contained characteristics in common with Ventrue, Lasombra and Cappadocian blood, suggesting that Irad sired the Antediluvians of those clans.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T12:24:12-07:00","id":1395424,"title":"","content":"I prefer Mithras as a 4th generation sired by Ventrue as he has much more panache than some of the 4th generation sired by the Ventrue Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> Mind you, Matthew Dawkins finds the idea of Mithras being a 4th or 5th originally FASCINATING and constantly makes the joke about being JUST about to tell us at the end of his podcasts.<br /> <br /> Which means that HE is actually Mithras' sire!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T12:25:24-07:00","id":1395425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395299-who-do-you-think-mithras\u2019s-true-love-is?p=1395416#post1395416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He would have had to strengthen his blood again before siring Alexander and Antonius, however.<br /> <br /> Also, regarding the sire of the Ventrue Antediluvian, Alexander names Enoch however, it's worth pointing out that in DA V20, some vampires got their hands on what was likely Irad's vitae and it contained characteristics in common with Ventrue, Lasombra and Cappadocian blood, suggesting that Irad sired the Antediluvians of those clans.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If we go with genealogy I don't think you'll ever find a definitive answer about who sires who between the 2nd and 3rd generation. Even in books it's all in character speculation, although some &quot;facts&quot; are repeated more often than others, for example Saulot and Malkav being brothers sired by Enoch.<br /> <br /> I can tell you how I did things. In my games:<br /> <br /> Irad sired three times: Brujah, Lasombra and Ventrue (I like the idea the Ventrue trying to claim he was sired by Enoch are misguided and do so out of pride rather than factual knowledge)<br /> <br /> Zillah sired four times: Toreador, Nosferatu, Gangrel and Ravnos (I like the idea she took family members and turned them into her childer)<br /> <br /> Enoch sired six times: Assamite, Cappadocian, Salubri, Malkavian, Setite and Tzimisce (most of these have claimed to have been sired by Caine's &quot;first born&quot; and besides I like the idea the three sires of the Baali belong to the same proto bloodline)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T15:42:38-07:00","id":1395468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395299-who-do-you-think-mithras\u2019s-true-love-is?p=1395424#post1395424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer Mithras as a 4th generation sired by Ventrue as he has much more panache than some of the 4th generation sired by the Ventrue Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> Mind you, Matthew Dawkins finds the idea of Mithras being a 4th or 5th originally FASCINATING and constantly makes the joke about being JUST about to tell us at the end of his podcasts.<br /> <br /> Which means that HE is actually Mithras' sire!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do actually reveal the truth behind Mithras' sire and his Generation when he was Embraced, in this video.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/dQw4w9WgXcQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/dQw4w9WgXcQ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/dQw4w9WgXcQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/dQw4w9WgXcQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T18:26:33-07:00","id":1395495,"title":"","content":"BJD discusses sire of Mithras question and of course, leaves it to players<br /> <br /> For me it only has two options: Veddhartha or Mithras diableries. <br /> Veddhartha diableried Ventrue and embraced Mithras, Alexander and so on, then disguised as a 4th gens<br /> Or Mithras diableried a 4th gens","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T19:18:30-07:00","id":1395501,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t see any reason that Mithras couldn\u2019t have been Sired by the Ventrue Antediluvian. (I never heard of Maltheas and would just pretend he didn\u2019t exist.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T19:35:36-07:00","id":1395502,"title":"","content":"I figure every Antediluvian has as many names as Satan.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T20:38:31-07:00","id":1395516,"title":"","content":"Roger de Camden's love for Mithras is probably:<br /> <br /> 1 part the Blood Bond<br /> 1 part Presence 9 [and repeated exposures of it too]<br /> 1 part the fact Mithras is THAT charismatic<br /> 1 part Roger genuinely believing in the cult of Mithras' as well as its demigod<br /> <br /> **Long Thoughts on Solar Exalted, Mithras, and Vampire Methuselahs**<br /> <br /> One of the things I've always liked about their relationship is the fact that it kind of gets into that same sort of &quot;Solar Exalted: Gods or Monsters&quot; feeling in that when you're dealing with someone who has a Charisma of 9 and Charms that make him the greatest orator who ever lived, you don't really have much difference between &quot;fake&quot; and &quot;real&quot; emotions. Mind-control is more blunt and crude compared to what Mithras exerts on his followers.<br /> <br /> A house rule I employ with the Blood Bond is that most of the insanity and cruel stories about it stem from the cognitive dissonance it generates. I use another Exalted example w/ Lilith and Desus for basically how the Vampire Blood Bond typically works. Most vampires are abusive evil dickheads and so your mind has to rationalize how you can love someone while they treat you like shit. This results in your typical ghoul becoming the broken wreck of a human being that they tend to be. At least in my games.<br /> <br /> However, if you are able to show the slightest bit of kindness and/or have the Disciplines plus natural charisma to back it up, the Blood Bond just reinforces what is already there. As such if you ever do break the Blood Bond, you basically are just likely to take the artificial emotions as the same as your real ones. Yes, the Blood Bond is just chemicals but so is the majority of what you feel on some level [says the Progenitor].<br /> <br /> All beings love Mithras who meet him because at Presence 9, you no longer really deal with an objective reality the same way normal people do. You live like a Sidhe Lord and Solar Exalted did in the good (bad?) old days. You are the greatest being who ever lived and no one will ever disagree with that save another Solar Exalted/Ancient vampire. Camden is special to Mithras because the latter cares about him as his High Priest/Majordormo and batman (to use a WW1 term). He'll never be an equal but that doesn't mean his centuries of loyal service aren't appreciated. If they have shared blood and/or sex its almost immaterial to that deeper emotional bond of god and immortal prophet.<br /> <br /> Oddly, I would say this doesn't preclude Roger having his own lovers and followers. I could easily see him hooking up with Serena, for example, and it would in no way impact his relationship with Mithras. Their relationship would be wholly different.<br /> <br /> Similarly, so is Mithras' love for Kementiri, which is one of the few relationships where Mithras could conceivably be talking to an equal. Their passion is something I'd actually argue makes their relationship the most &quot;normal&quot; of Mithras because I can see jealousy, lust, anger, and other emotions that are almost...human. However, my take on them would be closer to Hera and Zeus because neither person could really stand someone they couldn't control completely but that is the source of the attraction simultaneously. It would be the perfect example of a couple that would visit for decades, make love, try to take over the world, plot against one another, make a half-hearted assassination attempt, breakup, disappear for centuries, and then fall in love all over again.<br /> <br /> That's at least how I would run it.<br /> <br /> I honestly wouldn't be surprised if Mithras is &quot;lovers&quot; with most of his cultists when he's up and around, sharing vitae with the Cult of Mithras' vampires by feeding on them and letting them feed on him--even without sex, the intimacy of the act would make them lovers--and also be a form of humiliation/submission for them. Mithras, even if he is the literal son of a god turned into a vampire, is still just a jumped up cult leader.<br /> <br /> Demanding his followers give up of themselves to please him is just another way to exert his power. I can easily imagine Mithras being a figure who demands abject supplication from his followers in a campaign willing to &quot;go there&quot; and have player characters comfortable with dealing with those kind of dark topics. You could easily have this be where the Queen of London develops a centuries long hatred for Mithras for the humiliation of making her just another cultist. One that could eventually combine with her mental fortitude + natural resentment and ambition to allow her to actively plot against him. Revenge required centuries of growing stronger plus Mithras lying in torpor for lengthy periods but it eventually came.<br /> <br /> Or you could play it traditionally romantic with him being briefly entertained by Queen Anne's strength.<br /> <br /> Shao Kahn: I LIKE FEMALES WITH FIRE!<br /> <br /> Up to your ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-10-2020, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg",